@startuml Enhanced Sandbox Environment Setup Sequence

!theme plain
title SABER Enhanced Docker Environment Setup - Permanent & Ephemeral Container Support

actor Agent
participant "SessionManager" as SM
participant "BenchmarkManager" as BM
participant "EpisodeManager" as EM_EP
participant "ExecutionManager" as EM
participant "SandboxEnvironmentManager" as SBMGR
participant "PermanentEnvironmentManager" as PMGR
participant "DockerSandboxEnvironment" as DSE
participant "Docker Compose" as DC
participant "Target Services" as TS

== Episode Initialization with Permanent & Ephemeral Environments ==

Agent -> SM: POST /session/{id}/start-benchmark\n{task_ids: ["dvwa_sql_injection"], episode_attempts: 1}
activate SM

SM -> BM: create_benchmark_session(session_id, task_ids)
activate BM

note over BM
BenchmarkManager creates benchmark session
and loads task configuration including
sandbox_environment and permanent_environment
specifications
end note

BM -> SM: benchmark_session
SM -> BM: start_benchmark(session_id, benchmark_session)
BM -> BM: get first task from benchmark_session
deactivate BM

SM -> EM: configure_for_task(session_id, task_object)
activate EM

note over EM
ExecutionManager extracts sandbox_environment
and permanent_environment from task object
and configures both ephemeral and permanent environments.
Sandbox environment spec includes:
- execution container config
- target services (if ephemeral)
- multi-network configuration
- resource limits
Permanent environment provides persistent services
end note

EM -> PMGR: ensure_permanent_environment_running(permanent_env_name)
activate PMGR

note over PMGR
PermanentEnvironmentManager checks if
permanent services are already running.
If not, starts them on the permanent network.
Services like persistent databases, monitoring
end note

PMGR -> EM: permanent_services_ready
deactivate PMGR

EM -> SBMGR: create_session_environment(session_id, sandbox_env_spec)
activate SBMGR

SBMGR -> DSE: new DockerSandboxEnvironment(session_id, sandbox_env_spec)
activate DSE

SM -> EM_EP: start_episode(session_id, task_id, initial_context)
activate EM_EP

EM_EP -> SM: episode_object
deactivate EM_EP

note over DSE
DockerSandboxEnvironment detects
multi-network configuration and
prepares Docker Compose setup with
connections to both isolated and permanent networks
end note

DSE -> DSE: analyze_environment_spec()
DSE -> DSE: is_multi_network() -> True

== Multi-Network Environment Setup ==

DSE -> DSE: generate_compose_config()

note over DSE
Generates docker-compose.yml with:
- execution container (red team tools)
- optional ephemeral services
- Network connections to both:
  * Episode-specific isolated network
  * Permanent bridge network (for shared services)
- Health checks and dependencies
end note

DSE -> DC: docker-compose up -d
activate DC

DSE -> PMGR: connect_to_permanent_network(execution_container)
activate PMGR

note over PMGR
Connects the execution container to the permanent
network so it can access persistent services like
shared databases, monitoring, or target applications
end note

PMGR -> DSE: network_connection_established
deactivate PMGR

note over DC, TS
Episode execution container now connected to:
1. Its own isolated network (episode-specific)
2. Permanent bridge network (shared services)
Can access both ephemeral and permanent services
end note
end note

DC -> DSE: Start execution container
note over DSE
Pentesting sandbox starts with:
- Network access to target services
- Pentesting tools available
- No external network access
- Ready for agent commands
end note

DC -> DC: Wait for all health checks
DC --> DSE: All services healthy
deactivate DC

DSE -> DSE: verify_environment_health()
DSE -> DSE: get_primary_container() -> execution container

DSE --> SBMGR: DockerSandboxEnvironment ready
deactivate DSE

SBMGR --> EM: Environment created successfully
deactivate SBMGR

EM --> TM: Execution environment ready
deactivate EM

TM -> TM: create_episode(task_id, session_id, environment)
TM --> SM: Episode created with multi-container environment
deactivate TM

SM --> Agent: 200 OK\n{episode_id, environment_info}
deactivate SM

== Agent Command Execution in Enhanced Environment ==

Agent -> SM: MCP tool call: execute_action("nmap dvwa_webapp")
activate SM

SM -> EM: execute_action(session_id, "nmap dvwa_webapp")
activate EM

EM -> SBMGR: get_session_environment(session_id)
activate SBMGR

SBMGR --> EM: DockerSandboxEnvironment
deactivate SBMGR

EM -> DSE: execute_command(["nmap", "dvwa_webapp"])
activate DSE

note over DSE
Command executes in primary container
(pentesting sandbox) with network access
to target services via Docker Compose
internal network
end note

DSE -> DSE: run_in_primary_container()
DSE --> EM: CommandResult(success=True, data="Host dvwa_webapp is up...")
deactivate DSE

EM --> SM: CommandResult
deactivate EM

SM --> Agent: MCP result with nmap output
deactivate SM

== Environment Cleanup ==

Agent -> SM: DELETE /session/{id}
activate SM

SM -> SBMGR: cleanup_session(session_id)
activate SBMGR

SBMGR -> DSE: stop()
activate DSE

DSE -> DC: docker-compose down --volumes
activate DC

DC -> TS: Stop and remove all containers
deactivate TS

DC -> DC: Remove networks and volumes
DC --> DSE: Environment cleaned up
deactivate DC

DSE --> SBMGR: Cleanup complete
deactivate DSE

SBMGR --> SM: Session cleaned up
deactivate SBMGR

SM --> Agent: 200 OK - Session terminated
deactivate SM

note over Agent, DC
Complete multi-container environment
including target services and execution
environment properly orchestrated and
cleaned up via Docker Compose
end note

@enduml
